 "notes": [
  "Verdict PASS = every phase writer READY 12/12 with offsets continuous and cursor items unchanged, trust anchor moved both ways (Query/Stream/Kafka refuse the other generation), burst gate PASS, teardown 0 left.",
  "OPEN OBSERVATION: phase D writer clone 'auth_protocol' shows 401 = 1 (also after the burst). The tool counted the bare substring '401' in the clone's log tail (it also matches numbers and millisecond timestamps); the line was removed with the clone at teardown, so it is not attributable. Query/Stream ' 401' = 0, UNAUTHENTICATED / CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED / STRICT_RESUME_REFUSAL / HANDOFF_RESUME_REQUIRED = 0 in every phase, writer READY 12/12 at the D steady check. Tool fixed after the run (whole-token match, matching lines kept); the window's R1 command uses the same whole-token pattern.",
  "Burst data volume: every 200 warmup returned at most 1 row (the isolated stack holds minutes of ETH data; why BAR warmups returned at most 1 row was not investigated), so the burst exercised admission/lanes/TLS/JWT under 64 concurrent requests at near-zero row volume; production-volume retention is the IDR-129 isolated A/B (361-445 MiB over 12 bursts vs 472 -> 683).",
  "Burst statuses per burst: ~50 x 200, 23-25 OPEN_SEQUENCE_GAP, 0-6 DATA_NOT_READY, 103-109 RATE_LIMITED retries; 14-15 of 64 slices unresolved after 4 rounds (reported, not gated). The driver uses the TS consumer identity, so it shares that identity's quota with the writer clone; the writer clone was READY in 5/6, 1/7, 6/6 samples during the bursts (cause not verified; quota sharing is the likely one). In production the burst is the writer's own.",
  "Steady ready_all_samples false in C and D: the first samples fall into the STRICT start-up (as in the 2026-10-19 first run); last sample READY 12/12.",
  "Outage longer than the first run (251-291 s): B 312 s, C 519 s, D 353 s; the DL part (Query READY over mTLS) was 145-162 s after the broker recreate in every phase; the spread is the writer clone BOOTSTRAP (68-251 s to READY) under its 0.35 vCPU cap."
